{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withRecordingTracker"},{"text":" makes a tracker, binds it to the current task with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withTracker"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length of its body, then finishes it and returns a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"},{"text":" of every event tracked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"through it. Each call makes its own tracker, so tests that run at once never see each other’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events. Events tracked after the body returns, by work it started but didn’t wait for, are dropped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There are four spellings. The body can be synchronous or asynchronous, and it can take the tracker"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a parameter, for code that is handed its tracker (a SwiftUI view given it with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracker(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UIKit view controller given it as a trait) rather than reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.current"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A recording holds what the body returned, every record with its timestamp, source location and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context, each event’s name, and the events of one type through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording\/events(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the product to test targets only. To check a tracking plan from a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlanTesting"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import Testing","import TrackerTesting","","@Test func checkingOutTracksTheCartSize() async {","    let tracked = await withRecordingTracker { tracker in","        tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))","        return \"done\"","    }","    #expect(tracked.value == \"done\")","    #expect(tracked.names == [\"CheckoutStarted\"])","    #expect(tracked.events(of: CheckoutStarted.self).map(\\.cartSize) == [3])","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/testingwhatyoutrack","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers views, view controllers and asynchronous code."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"TrackerTesting"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"TrackerTesting","role":"collection","title":"TrackerTesting"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-8blfh","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-mlec","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-26pul","doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/withRecordingTracker(_:)-pnmv"],"title":"Recording a body’s events","anchor":"Recording-a-bodys-events"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TrackerTesting\/documentation\/TrackerTesting\/TrackerRecording"],"title":"Reading what was tracked","anchor":"Reading-what-was-tracked"}],"variants":[{"p